    "narrative": "The primary focus for today\u2019s lineup is maximizing stolen base potential and exploiting soft matchups, leading to **Corbin Carroll** standing out as our clear-cut elite play with a score of 85.94. His massive projection is bolstered by the high-upside matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano, whose 4.80 xERA provides the perfect runway for **Corbin Carroll** to utilize his elite sprint speed and capitalize on the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery. Complementing this, **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Seiya Suzuki** also grade out as strong plays near the 70.0 mark; **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits significantly from the SP skill gap against Walker Buehler, while **Seiya Suzuki** maintains his value despite a wind-in warning due to his advantageous platoon split and the favorable 4.97 xERA of the opposing starter.\n\nOur roster construction heavily rewards the speed-first profile, with **Brice Turang** and **Mickey Moniak** both earning starting spots for their ability to pressure the basepaths. The most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 43.54. While **Kyle Karros** offers solid utility, he was displaced by the higher overall efficiency of **Josh Naylor** and the platoon-neutral power floor provided by the rest of our corner infielders. We continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, and **James Wood**; while these players are locked into their positions, any last-minute defensive swaps or pinch-hitting risks could shift our leverage. With **Vinnie Pasquantino** facing a tougher test against Logan Gilbert\u2019s 3.03 xERA, we are relying on our depth\u2014including **Trevor Story**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**\u2014to remain ready should the game flow dictate late-inning substitutions.",
